            <div xml:id="d585">

                <pb facs="0731" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2260: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Warren</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-06T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                                1921—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>178. Inform Japanese Foreign Office that this Government has suggested to John F.
                    Stevens the advisability of his being in Washington at the time of the Armament
                    Conference in order that his special knowledge of the affairs of the Chinese
                    Eastern Railway may be directly available, and that this Government is informed
                    that Mr. Stevens is planning to come. The Department has approved Stevens’
                    suggestion that he appoint Colonel Johnson President <hi rendition="#italic">pro
                        tempore</hi> of the Technical Board.</p>
                <p>Cable Stevens as soon as you have done this and advise him that Department
                    approves appointment of Johnson and that he may now make his plans public.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
